Sval: The address bar's rows teach their keys, and its sections are groups

Each row of the Launcher shows what Enter does on it and the line under the
list what its modifiers do, an open tab of another workspace shows that
workspace as a chip, and a screen reader hears each section as a group
named by its heading, and each open tab with its workspace (launcher spec
§7, §8). The view draws its rows itself and offers no hook for either, so
it hands its rows to `SvalLauncherRows` once it has laid them out and
labelled them (`#updateIndices`), and again when the selection moves
(`#selectElement`).

